<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" elementFormDefault="qualified" attributeFormDefault="unqualified">
  <xs:annotation>
    <xs:documentation>
RESPONSE schema for customerCertificateSearch (Customer360). Returned in the response body.
Audited 2026-10-12 against the loyalty-app service generation.

In the loyalty-app service generation this operation is served by the second-generation
("B") certificate search (alias operation name customerCertificateSearchB). The response
therefore groups coupons under LOYALTY_COUPONS and MARKETING_COUPONS. The earlier published
schema described the first-generation shape (TRANSACTION elements directly under RESPONSE,
with the misspelled COUPON_REDEMED_DATE); that shape is NOT returned by this operation in the
loyalty-app service generation.

Response shapes (all use a bare RESPONSE root):
  1. Success      -- RESPONSE_DATE, CUSTOMER_ID, LOYALTY_ID, LOYALTY_DATE, BALANCE_LOYALTY_POINTS,
                     then LOYALTY_COUPONS and/or MARKETING_COUPONS. NO RESPONSE_CODE on success.
  2. Early error  -- RESPONSE_DATE + RESPONSE_CODE only (E101-E104, E110, E111, E127, E899, E999).
  3. Late error   -- RESPONSE_DATE, the four customer elements, then RESPONSE_CODE
                     (E121 no coupons, E136, E137).

RESPONSE_CODE catalog (kept as xs:string on purpose; new codes must not break validation):
  E101 XmlInput empty       E102 malformed XML      E103 parser configuration   E104 I/O reading input
  E110 CUSTOMER_ID missing or empty        E111 customer not found or not enabled
  E121 no coupons matched                  E127 STORE_ID unknown
  E136 COUPON_PROMO_TYPE not one of C7, LOYALTY, C3, MARKETING, ALL
  E137 COUPON_STATUS not one of AVAILABLE, REDEEMED, AUDITED, FUTURE, EXPIRED, ALL
  E899 accessTokenKey validation failed
  E999 unhandled error (RESPONSE_DATE is an EMPTY element and there is no ResponseId)

All timestamps are "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.S" strings (e.g. 2026-10-12 15:00:02.123), NOT
xs:dateTime, and are emitted as EMPTY elements when the underlying date is not set.
    </xs:documentation>
  </xs:annotation>

  <!-- Shared shape of a coupon row under LOYALTY_COUPONS and MARKETING_COUPONS. The service emits all nine elements, in this order, for every row. -->
  <xs:complexType name="CertificateTransaction">
    <xs:sequence>
      <xs:element name="CUSTOMER_DESCRIPTION" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Description stored on the coupon; empty when none is stored.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="COUPON_NUMBER" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>The coupon (certificate) number.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="COUPON_VALUE" type="xs:decimal" minOccurs="0">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Always a whole number (no decimals). For loyalty coupons: the redeemed value recorded for this customer's coupon, rounded half-up to a whole number, or 0 when none is recorded. Always 0 for marketing coupons.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="COUPON_STATUS" minOccurs="0">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Current status of the coupon. These five values are the complete set the service emits for this element.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
        <xs:simpleType>
          <xs:restriction base="xs:NMTOKEN">
            <xs:enumeration value="COUPON_AVAILABLE">
              <xs:annotation>
                <xs:documentation>Issued, unused, and within its validity window.</xs:documentation>
              </xs:annotation>
            </xs:enumeration>
            <xs:enumeration value="COUPON_UNAVAILABLE">
              <xs:annotation>
                <xs:documentation>Issued and unused, but its start date is still in the future.</xs:documentation>
              </xs:annotation>
            </xs:enumeration>
            <xs:enumeration value="COUPON_EXPIRED">
              <xs:annotation>
                <xs:documentation>Unused and past its end date.</xs:documentation>
              </xs:annotation>
            </xs:enumeration>
            <xs:enumeration value="COUPON_REDEEMED">
              <xs:annotation>
                <xs:documentation>The coupon has been scanned at a POS.</xs:documentation>
              </xs:annotation>
            </xs:enumeration>
            <xs:enumeration value="COUPON_AUDITED">
              <xs:annotation>
                <xs:documentation>The redemption has been reconciled against an order.</xs:documentation>
              </xs:annotation>
            </xs:enumeration>
          </xs:restriction>
        </xs:simpleType>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="COUPON_EXPIRY_DATE" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>End of validity, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.S". When the coupon has no end date the service returns its start date plus 120 days; empty when it has neither.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="COUPON_REDEEMED_DATE" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>When the coupon was scanned at a POS, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.S"; empty if never scanned. Correctly spelled in this operation.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="COUPON_AUDITED_DATE" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>When the redemption was reconciled against an order, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.S"; empty if not reconciled.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="COUPON_ISSUE_DATE" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>When the coupon was issued, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.S"; empty if not recorded.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="START_DATE" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Start of validity, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.S"; empty if not set.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
    </xs:sequence>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:element name="RESPONSE">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>Response payload carrying the customer's loyalty context and the matching coupons, or an error code.</xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:sequence>
        <xs:element name="RESPONSE_DATE" type="xs:string">
          <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>Server timestamp, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.S". Always the first element. Deliberately xs:string: the format is not ISO 8601. Empty on E999.</xs:documentation>
          </xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
        <!-- Repeating choice: RESPONSE_CODE directly follows RESPONSE_DATE on early errors but follows the customer elements on late errors (E121, E136, E137). -->
        <xs:choice minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
          <xs:element name="RESPONSE_CODE" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>Outcome code; ABSENT on success. See the catalog in the schema header.</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element name="CUSTOMER_ID" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>Customer identifier the results belong to (echo of the request).</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element name="LOYALTY_ID" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>The customer's loyalty program identifier; empty when the customer is not enrolled.</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element name="LOYALTY_DATE" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>When the loyalty identifier was recorded for the customer, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.S"; empty when the customer is not enrolled.</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element name="BALANCE_LOYALTY_POINTS" type="xs:string">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>Current loyalty point balance (earned minus redeemed) as a whole-number string, may be negative; EMPTY when the customer is not enrolled.</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element name="LOYALTY_COUPONS">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>Coupons belonging to loyalty promotions. Present only when at least one such coupon matched.</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
            <xs:complexType>
              <xs:sequence>
                <xs:element name="TRANSACTION" type="CertificateTransaction" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
              </xs:sequence>
            </xs:complexType>
          </xs:element>
          <xs:element name="MARKETING_COUPONS">
            <xs:annotation>
              <xs:documentation>Coupons belonging to any promotion type other than loyalty. Present only when at least one such coupon matched. Follows LOYALTY_COUPONS when both are present.</xs:documentation>
            </xs:annotation>
            <xs:complexType>
              <xs:sequence>
                <xs:element name="TRANSACTION" type="CertificateTransaction" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
              </xs:sequence>
            </xs:complexType>
          </xs:element>
        </xs:choice>
      </xs:sequence>
      <xs:attribute name="ResponseId" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Request-log correlation id generated by the service for this call. Present on every response except E999.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:attribute>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="WEBSERVICE">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>Gate-error envelope of the older service generation: when the tenant key (E888) or the access token (E899) is rejected before the operation runs, the response is WEBSERVICE / RESPONSE / RESPONSE_CODE only - no RESPONSE_DATE and no ResponseId. The loyalty-app service generation returns the same errors as a bare RESPONSE root with RESPONSE_DATE and RESPONSE_CODE.</xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:sequence>
        <xs:element name="RESPONSE">
          <xs:complexType>
            <xs:sequence>
              <xs:element name="RESPONSE_DATE" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0"/>
              <xs:element name="RESPONSE_CODE" type="xs:string"/>
            </xs:sequence>
            <xs:attribute name="ResponseId" type="xs:string"/>
          </xs:complexType>
        </xs:element>
      </xs:sequence>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
</xs:schema>
